    "result_text": "All 264 tests pass \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**. (The lone `ERROR ... POST /api/users` line is an existing test that intentionally exercises the 500 handler, unrelated to this change.)\n\n## Summary\n\nThe 400/409/429 rejections in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` were returning bare `ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.X)` with **no body**, bypassing the existing `ProblemDetail`-based advice. I routed them through the central advice so they now emit RFC7807 `application/problem+json`.\n\n**New exception types** (`rest/advice/`), each mapping to a fixed status:\n- `BadRequestException` \u2192 400\n- `ConflictException` \u2192 409\n- `RateLimitExceededException` \u2192 429\n\n**`ExceptionControllerAdvice`** \u2014 added three `@ExceptionHandler` methods that reuse the existing `detailBuild(...)` helper, producing a `ProblemDetail` with `type`, `title`, `status`, and `detail`. Spring automatically serializes `ResponseEntity<ProblemDetail>` with the `application/problem+json` content type (verified by the existing `AcceptanceTest`, which asserts exactly that on the validation path using the same code path).\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 replaced the eight bare rejection returns with `throw`s carrying a specific `detail` message for each cause (invalid address / telephone / email / postcode / future registration date; city-capacity conflict; duplicate-identity conflict; daily-limit rate cap).\n\nHTTP status codes are unchanged; the pre-existing `MethodArgumentNotValidException` 400 handler and its problem body were untouched.",
